# Gilgamesh, Master-at-Arms: "Whenever Gilgamesh enters or attacks, look at the top six cards of your library. You may put any number of Equipment
# cards from among them onto the battlefield. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order. When you put one or more Equipment
# onto the battlefield this way, you may attach one of them to a Samurai you control." Ruling: the reflexive ability can't try to attach an
# Equipment to a creature it can't legally be attached to.
# Turn 1: Gilgamesh enters; Bot1 puts no card onto the battlefield, the Loxodon Warhammer included, so the reflexive ability does not trigger.
# Turn 3: Giver of Runes gives Gilgamesh, Bot1's only Samurai, protection from colorless, and he attacks. Skullclamp and Bark of Doran (white)
# are put onto the battlefield; Skullclamp can be attached to no Samurai Bot1 controls and is not offered, and Bark of Doran is attached to
# Gilgamesh, a 6/7 that deals 7 (Bark's "assigns combat damage equal to its toughness"). Bot1 then casts Colleen Wing, Street Samurai.
# Turn 5: Gilgamesh is protected from colorless again and attacks. Paradise Mantle is put onto the battlefield; Neither Gilgamesh nor Giver of
# Runes (a creature, not a Samurai) is offered for it, and it goes to Colleen Wing. Turn 7: Lavaspur Boots is put onto the battlefield and Bot1 attaches nothing.

